log * Jump to start: press Ctrl+Home
check abiword/abiword-check-005.png
# Warm-up open of the Zoom dialog, discarded with Escape.
#
# The FIRST Zoom dialog of a session is the one that races: AbiWord sometimes
# maps it before setting WM_TRANSIENT_FOR, and fluxbox then applies the
# [app] (name=abiword) rule from pin-windows.sh to it - [Deco]{NONE} plus
# [Position](TOPLEFT){0 0} - so it comes up 162x259 at 0,0 instead of 178x259
# at 1,45. Every coordinate below is measured against the 1,45 form, so in the
# racing case all four of them miss: the Percent radio is never selected, the
# 150 goes nowhere, and Close at 130,261 falls 3 px BELOW a dialog that ends at
# y=258. The dialog then stays open across the menu bar at 0,0 and swallows the
# two View clicks of the second traversal, so the zoom never leaves Page Width
# and check-006 fails on a page-width screen. Observed twice: once on the
# measurement node (rmse 0.225042, dialog stacked under the main window) and
# once locally (rmse 0.279954, dialog stacked over it).
#
# Every open after the first has come up 1,45 178x259 - eight observations
# across four sessions - so opening one and throwing it away moves the risky
# first creation to a point where nothing depends on where it lands.
#
# Escape, not a click on Close: the two forms' Close buttons overlap by about
# 4 px, so no single coordinate closes both, whereas a key goes to whichever
# window has focus wherever it sits.
